# A [[pregnant]] [[woman]], especially one [[expecting]] her [[first]] [[child]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2000|author=Allison England|title=Aromatherapy and Massage for Mother and Baby|pageurl=http://books.google.com/books?id=8y4_rXN3dqIC&pg=PA52|page=52|publisher=Healing Arts Press|year_published=2000|isbn=0892818980
|passage=The ideal position for a back massage for the '''mother-to-be''' is to sit astride a chair supported by cushions.}}
# A [[woman]] whose [[partner]] is [[pregnant]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2010|author=Amie Klempnauer Miller|title=She Looks Just Like You: A Memoir of (Nonbiological Lesbian) Motherhood|pageurl=http://books.google.com/books?id=XQu4cU8A2z4C&pg=PT62|page=55|publisher=Beacon Press|year_published=2010|isbn=9780807004692
|passage=I don't know how other lesbian, nonbiological '''mothers-to-be''', who tried to get pregnant and could not, might experience their partners' pregnancy.}}

